  <result aggregation-status="1" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 3: National, Regional and multinational bodies take concrete steps to improve POC at international, national, and local levels.</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sub-result: International or regional multinational bodies take concrete, progressive actions to strengthen civilian protection at international, national, and local levels as a result of direct substantive engagement with conflict-affected communities and civilians (E.g., policies, training, reviews, doctrine, SOPs, etc.)Sub-result: International or regional multinational bodies adopt public positions, actions and approaches that establish, reinforce, or improve standards for the protection of civilians in conflict (E.g. through reports, public statements, mandates, policies, votes, strategic reviews, etc.)Sub-result: International or regional bodies, including their field presences on the ground, take concrete steps to improve the protection of civilians and communities in conflict-affected countries (E.g. through diplomacy, programs, policies, training, capacities, mechanisms, or the conduct of multilateral security forces.)</narrative>
   </description>
